A carve of lines or shares takes any range, not only one within the invoked capability.
It would hand out lines or shares the carver does not hold, or ones there are not;
a capability to lines or shares names ones there are, within its parent's.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: share capability outside the shares there are

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -471,9 +471,6 @@ static int carve_range(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap, c
 {
     uint32_t off = arg[1];
     uint32_t len = arg[2];
-    if (len == 0 || off > cap->b || len > cap->b - off) {
-        return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
-    }
     struct cap sub = { .type = cap->type, .rights = cap->rights, .a = cap->a + off, .b = len };
     return cap_store(thread_table(t), arg[3], &sub, slot_node(t, slot));
 }
